# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Test scratch space (kept inside the repo for sandboxed runs)
.pytest_tmp/
.pytest_cache/

# Scratch left behind by build_submission.py (staged weight copies)
/outputs/staging/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Too large for GitHub - a size limit, NOT a privacy decision
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB, and that limit applies to private
# repositories too. These nine files therefore stay local; back them up on an
# external drive or object storage, or move them to Git LFS (not installed
# here, and the free tier's 1 GB does not cover the ~5.6 GB they need).
#
# NOTE: a bare `data/` pattern also matches src/data/ and silently dropped two
# load-bearing modules (coco.py, split_by_source.py) from the first published
# commit. Always anchor directory patterns with a leading slash.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore has no inline comments - a trailing `# 553 MB` becomes part
# of the pattern and the rule silently stops matching. Keep comments on their
# own lines.
#
#   /data/raw/训练集A.zip                          553 MB
#   /outputs/checkpoints/                          6 x 335 MB
#   /outputs/submissions/submission*/solution.zip  2 x 1.5 GB
/data/raw/训练集A.zip
/outputs/checkpoints/
/outputs/submissions/submission*/solution.zip
solution/model/*.pt

# Everything else is tracked - including the competition data, the frozen
# official scripts and the assistant's project notes. This repository is
# private and holds no credentials (checked by a project-wide scan).

# OS
.DS_Store
